# Reserved golden-master TEST-DATA folder (authorized by NY4I, 2026-07-05).
#
# The repo root ignores *.TRW / *.CFG and log exports on purpose, so nobody
# ever commits real operating logs. The curated regression fixtures HERE are the
# one sanctioned exception: re-include them for this subtree only. Everywhere
# else in the repo, the root ignores still apply unchanged.
# log.db -- THE FIXTURE since 2026-09-24.  The corpus's input is the contest
# log itself; see corpus-lib.sh for NY4I's decision.  Nothing in the root
# ignores *.db today, and this says so on purpose: a rule added there later
# must not silently drop thirteen regression inputs.
!*.db

# log.cfg -- the contest DEFINITION, and no longer an input to the golden run.
# test-adif-roundtrip.sh needs it to create a fresh empty contest of the right
# type before importing a ref.adi.
!*.cfg
!*.CFG

# NO .trw LIVES HERE ANY MORE.  The six D7 binary logs that are still needed
# are unit fixtures, in tr4w/test/unit/fixtures/binarylog -- that is where
# reading a D7 log is covered now.  These two lines stay so a stray operating
# log dropped in this subtree is still visible rather than silently ignored.
!*.trw
!*.TRW
!*.adi
!*.ADI
!*.cbr
!*.CBR

# D12 candidate exports are transient golden_diff inputs, regenerated each
# run from the D12 build -- outputs to compare, not fixtures to track.
cand.adi
cand.cbr

# So is the export named after the log itself. The !*.adi/!*.ADI above is a
# BLANKET re-include: it readmits every ADIF in this subtree, artifacts
# included, which is how a 375 KB log.ADI came to be sitting beside a ref.adi
# as an untracked file nobody had noticed (2026-08-26). Only ref.* is a
# fixture here; everything else an export run drops is transient.
log.adi
log.ADI
log.cbr
log.CBR

# The staged export's own database is NOT written here -- the run stages into
# build-out/corpus-work -- but a hand-run export in this directory would leave
# a <stem>.db and a -wal beside the fixture.  log.db is the fixture; anything
# else with that extension is transient.
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
